GRADE-LEVEL CALIBRATION (LehrplanPLUS Bayern)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════

Adjust vocabulary, complexity ceiling, and allowed constructs strictly to the grade. Two tracks exist from Jgst. 11 onward: NTG (continued) and "spaet beginnend" (late-start). The input specifies the track.

── Jgst. 9 — NTG — PROGRAMMING ENTRY ──
  Curriculum: OOP introduction (objects, classes, attributes, methods, constructors), control structures (if/else, for, while), variables & data types, simple arrays, associations.
  Prior knowledge: OO modeling from Jgst. 6–7 (diagrams, no code). Spreadsheet functions/data flows (Lernbereich 1). Basic SQL (SELECT/FROM/WHERE).
  Allowed constructs: Sequenz, Selektion (if/else), Wiederholung (for, while), simple methods with parameters and return, basic array access, object instantiation.
  NOT yet known: inheritance, polymorphism, recursion, ArrayList, sorting algorithms, nested loops beyond trivial use.
  Max LOC highest tier: 14.

── Jgst. 10 — NTG — OOP & DATA STRUCTURES ──
  Curriculum: Arrays/Lists (indexed access, iteration), advanced OOP (Assoziation, Aggregation, Vererbung/Generalisierung, Polymorphismus ansatzweise), Sequenzdiagramme, Zustandsdiagramme, basic sorting/searching algorithms.
  Prior knowledge: everything from Jgst. 9 + SQL with JOINs + OOP basics.
  Allowed constructs: all of Jgst. 9 + inheritance, method overriding (basic), nested loops, sorting algorithms (Selection Sort, Insertion Sort), searching in arrays/lists.
  NOT yet known: recursion, linked lists, trees, graphs, Stack/Queue as ADT.
  Max LOC highest tier: 18.

── Jgst. 11 — NTG — GRAPHS, CODING, AI ──
  Curriculum: Graphs (BFS, Dijkstra, Adjazenzmatrix), Codierung & Verschluesselung (binary/hex, Caesar cipher, public-key principle), KI (k-NN or decision tree, Perzeptron), Projekt.
  Prior knowledge: everything from Jgst. 9–10.
  Allowed constructs: all of Jgst. 10 + graph traversal, matrix operations, 2D arrays, more complex OOP.
  NOT yet known: recursion (comes Jgst. 12), linked lists, trees, formal languages.
  Max LOC highest tier: 20.

── Jgst. 11 — SPAET BEGINNEND — PROGRAMMING ENTRY ──
  Curriculum: Introduction to algorithms and programming (variables, types, if/else, loops), simple search/sort algorithms, possibly visual programming (Scratch).
  Prior knowledge: NONE in programming. Basic IT literacy only.
  Allowed constructs: variables, if/else, for/while loops, simple functions, basic arrays.
  NOT yet known: OOP, inheritance, recursion, complex data structures.
  Treat like Jgst. 9 NTG for complexity calibration.
  Max LOC highest tier: 14.

── Jgst. 12 — GRUNDLEGEND — RECURSION & DYNAMIC DATA STRUCTURES ──
  Curriculum: Rekursion (linear + verzweigt: ggT, Fibonacci, Hanoi, Fraktale), Tiefensuche (DFS), einfach verkettete Liste (Kompositum-Pattern, Stack, Queue), Binaerbaum (Suchbaum, Traversierungen: Inorder/Preorder/Postorder), Informationssicherheit, Nebenlaeufigkeit (Grundlagen).
  Prior knowledge: everything from Jgst. 9–11 NTG.
  Allowed constructs: all previous + recursion, linked list operations, tree traversal, recursive data structures.
